  "query_preview": "..\n(Tuesday through Saturday)\nIssued at 1258 PM CST Sun Nov 1 2026\n\nA fast paced but subdued alternating ridging/troughing mid to \nupper air pattern sets in within more zonal flow behind the \nPacific cold front and associated mid to upper air system. This \nmaintains highs within the mid 60s to mid 70s F and lows within \nthe 40s to lower 50s F each day/night, as well as very low (less \nthan 10%) rain chances. Dew point temperatures largely settle in \nthe 40s F, drier than what we've experienced since summer and \nenough to result in diurnal variation of at least 20F-25F. Coupled\nwith longer nights and clearer skies, the seasonal pattern will \nfeel very attuned with the calendar, bringing the first real \nconsistent cooler weather of autumn to the area. Frost will be \npossible on cooler nights for higher elevations of the Marfa \nPlateau, slowly putting an end to this year's growing season for \nthat region.",
